      "text": "To find the smallest positive integer that is both an integer power of 11 and is not a palindrome, we need to evaluate the powers of 11 starting from the smallest positive integers and check if the resulting number is a palindrome.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the first few powers of 11:\n\n\\[\n11^1 = 11\n\\]\n\\[\n11^2 = 121\n\\]\n\\[\n11^3 = 1331\n\\]\n\\[\n11^4 = 14641\n\\]\n\nNow, we will check if these numbers are palindromes. A palindrome is a number that reads the same forwards and backwards.\n\n- The number 11 is a single-digit palindrome.\n- The number 121 is a three-digit palindrome (1, 2, 1).\n- The number 1331 is a four-digit palindrome (1, 3, 3, 1).\n- The number 14641 is a five-digit palindrome (1, 4, 6, 4, 1).\n\nSince all these numbers are palindromes, we need to check the next power of 11.\n\nNext, let's calculate \\(11^5\\):\n\n\\[\n11^5 = 11 \\times 11 \\times 11 \\times 11 \\times 11\n\\]\n\nTo simplify this, we can break it down step-by-step:\n\n\\[\n11^2 = 121\n\\]\n\\[\n11^4 = 121 \\times 121 = 14641\n\\]\n\\[\n11^5 = 11^2 \\times 11^3 = 121 \\times 14641\n\\]\n\nNow, let's calculate \\(11^5\\):\n\n\\[\n11^5 = 11 \\times 11 \\times 11 \\times 11 \\times 11 = 1331 \\times 19448 = 25937444\n\\]\n\nWe need to check if 25937444 is a palindrome. To do this, we reverse the digits of 25937444:\n\n\\[\n25937444 \\rightarrow 44473952\n\\]\n\nSince 25937444 does not read the same forwards and backwards, it is not a palindrome.\n\nTherefore, the smallest positive integer that is both an integer power of 11 and is not a palindrome is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1331}\n\\]",
